{
  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted fusion) achieved 72.5% accuracy at 3.60 GPU hours, giving us a single data point in a high-capacity region of the search space. The most important immediate question is whether the weighted fusion mechanism is actually contributing over a simpler concatenation, since all other components (encoders, aggregation, profile setting) are identical. This experiment (config_003) is a controlled A/B test changing only fusion from weighted to concat, directly testing whether the current best can be improved or confirmed. If concat matches or exceeds weighted, it opens a cheaper/simpler design axis; if weighted clearly wins, we can lock in that choice and explore other dimensions (RNA encoder, image encoder, aggregation) in subsequent experiments. This is the best use of experiment 2 because it exploits the one strong signal we have with a minimal, interpretable change rather than jumping to a very different architecture, and it reduces uncertainty about a core design choice before we spend remaining budget on broader exploration. Expected relative cost: approximately equal to config_001 (~3.5–3.7 GPU hours), since the architecture and encoders are identical and only the fusion head differs."
}

